PlateMatch — License Plate Social Review App

A mobile app (React Native / Expo) where you can scan a license plate, rate
the driver 0-5 stars, tag them with emoji labels, and leave notes (like
"broken tail light"). Plate owners can claim their plate to see their
reputation.

QUICK START
-----------

1. Install dependencies
   npm install

2. Copy environment file and fill in credentials
   cp .env.example .env

3. Set up Supabase
   - Create a free project at https://supabase.com
   - Run supabase/schema.sql in the Supabase SQL editor
   - Copy the project URL and anon key into .env

4. (Optional) Set up PlateRecognizer
   - Get a free API key at https://platerecognizer.com (500 lookups/month free)
   - Add it to .env
   - Without a key, the app runs in demo mode with a mock plate

5. Start the app
   npm start
   Press 'i' for iOS simulator, 'a' for Android emulator, or scan the QR
   code with Expo Go on your phone.

ARCHITECTURE
------------

  app/                  Expo Router screens (file-based routing)
  app/(tabs)/           Tab bar screens (Home, My Plates)
  app/auth.tsx          Sign in / sign up modal
  app/camera.tsx        Plate scanning screen
  app/plate/[id].tsx    Plate detail + reviews
  app/rate/[id].tsx     Rate a driver (modal)
  app/claim/[id].tsx    Claim a plate (modal)
  components/           Shared UI components
  lib/                  Supabase client, plate API, data access
  types/                TypeScript types and tag definitions
  supabase/schema.sql   Database schema (run once in Supabase SQL editor)

KEY DECISIONS
-------------

Plate OCR: PlateRecognizer API (platerecognizer.com) — specialized license
plate OCR with US state detection. Falls back to demo mode without a key.

Ownership Verification: Claims marked pending (unverified). Two people
claiming the same plate triggers "conflicted" status for manual review.
Future: request registration document photo to raise the bar.

Anonymous Reviews: Username hidden on public page, but account link kept
internally for moderation.

Privacy Roadmap: rate-limiting per reviewer per plate, report/flag system,
minimum account age, geofencing to reduce stalking surface.
